  {
   "id": "oDTZFN2MCwAJ",
   "from": "Dennis Murphy",
   "author": "0c39e60ddb38622b",
   "date": "2015-10-25T08:01:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: geom_line plots bars?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">For the first time, I got an error when reading data from dput(), but I figured out that the problem was that you made month (mes) a factor and tried to construct lines across its levels. It can be done, but you need to set a group aesthetic on device.category in order to get it. I scaled down your data and chose to plot it with respect to a created date variable, whereby I could manufacture a custom axis label for the date. Pardon my non-Unicode naming scheme :)<div><br></div><div><div>d3 &lt;- data.frame(ano = rep(c(2014, 2015), times = c(12, 27)),</div><div>         mes = c(7L, 7L, 8L, 9L, 9L, 10L, 10L, 10L, 11L, </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>     11L, 12L, 12L, 1L, 1L, 2L, 2L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 4L, 4L, 4L, 5L, </div><div>     5L, 6L, 6L, 6L, 7L, 7L, 7L, 8L, 8L, 8L, 9L, 9L, 9L, 10L, </div><div>     10L, 10L),</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>         device.category = factor(c(1L, 2L, 1L, 1L, </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>     2L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 3L, </div><div>     1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L, 1L, </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>     2L, 3L, 1L, 2L, 3L), levels = 1L:3L, labels = c(&quot;desktop&quot;, &quot;mobile&quot;,</div><div>     &quot;tablet&quot;)),</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>         sesiones = c(58L, 1L, 7L, 33L, 3L, </div><div>     47L, 4L, 2L, 11L, 2L, 47L, 2L, 48L, 2L, 18L, 4L, 248L, 7L, </div><div>     2L, 309L, 7L, 1L, 543L, 7L, 100L, 18L, 2L, 138L, 30L, 2L, </div><div>     118L, 35L, 3L, 135L, 46L, 3L, 89L, 49L, 2L))</div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>d3$date &lt;- as.Date(with(d3, paste(ano, mes, &quot;01&quot;, sep = &quot;-&quot;)))</div><div><br></div><div>library(ggplot2)</div><div>library(scales)</div><div>ggplot(d3, aes(x = date, y = sesiones, color = device.category)) +</div><div>     theme_bw() +</div><div>     geom_point() + geom_line(size = 1) +</div><div>     scale_x_date(labels = date_format(&quot;%b\\n%Y&quot;)) +</div><div>     theme(legend.position = c(1, 1), </div><div>           legend.justification = c(&quot;right&quot;, &quot;top&quot;))</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I put the legend inside the plot region in order to provide more room for the graph. If you just want the month names, change the argument of date_format() to &quot;%b&quot;. To get every month labeled (without year), try</div><div><br></div><div><div>ggplot(d3, aes(x = date, y = sesiones, color = device.category)) +</div><div>     theme_bw() +</div><div>     geom_point() + geom_line(size = 1) +</div><div>     scale_x_date(breaks = seq(as.Date(&quot;2014-07-01&quot;), as.Date(&quot;2015-10-01&quot;), </div><div>                               by = &quot;month&quot;),</div><div>                  labels = date_format(&quot;%b&quot;)) +</div><div>     theme(legend.position = c(1, 1), </div><div>           legend.justification = c(&quot;right&quot;, &quot;top&quot;))</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>As for your original attempts, there are some problems:</div><div><br></div><div>1. Since you defined mes as an (ordered) factor, geom_line() will not work by itself since it requires a numeric x-variable. When given a factor, it silently ignores the call. You need to set a group = aesthetic before geom_line() will work. But...</div><div>2. You have repeat values of certain months over 2014 and 2015, so the plot that would get rendered is probably not what you would have expected, which is why I surmise you resorted to faceting by year.</div><div><br></div><div>Converting to Date format and specializing the date labels seems to be a reasonable compromise under the assumption that you really wanted a time plot. If instead you really wanted a month plot separated by year per product category, here&#39;s an alternative:</div><div><br></div><div># Convert month and year to factor</div><div><div>d3$mes2 &lt;- factor(d3$mes, levels = 1:12, labels = month.abb)</div><div>d3$ano2 &lt;- factor(d3$ano)</div><div><br></div><div>ggplot(d3, aes(x = mes2, y = sesiones, group = ano2, color = ano2)) +</div><div>    theme_bw() +</div><div>    geom_point() + geom_line(size = 1) +</div><div>    facet_wrap(~ device.category, ncol = 1, scales = &quot;free_y&quot;) +</div></div><div>    labs(x = &quot;mes&quot;, color = &quot;ano&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>Dennis</div><div><br></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Oct 24, 2015 at 7:26 PM, Omar André Gonzáles Díaz <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oma.go...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
